From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VyOS LS1046A <ask20@vyos-ls1046a-build>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman-port: size the 10G RX BMI FIFO from a module parameter (0179)

The 24 KB FIFO of a 10G receive port overflowed the MAC under bidirectional
line rate (mEMAC RDRP +3.7k per port in 30 s, about the retransmit count).
fsl_dpaa_fman.fsl_fm_rx10g_fifo_kb (24-112, default 80) sets it; vendor
review R12, plans/ASK2-VENDOR-ASK-REVIEW.md. Total BMI FIFO is 295 KB.

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
index 43469df..bf86486 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
@@ -1556,6 +1556,13 @@ static int get_dflt_extra_num_of_open_dmas(u8 major, enum fman_port_type type,
 	}
 }
 
+/* KB of BMI FIFO per 10G receive port. 24 KB overflowed the MAC under
+ * bidirectional line rate (RDRP counter, plans/ASK2-VENDOR-ASK-REVIEW.md R12).
+ */
+static uint fsl_fm_rx10g_fifo_kb = 80;
+module_param(fsl_fm_rx10g_fifo_kb, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(fsl_fm_rx10g_fifo_kb, "BMI FIFO per 10G RX port in KB (24-112, default 80)");
+
 static int get_dflt_num_of_fifo_bufs(u8 major, enum fman_port_type type,
 				     u16 speed)
 {
@@ -1571,7 +1578,7 @@ static int get_dflt_num_of_fifo_bufs(u8 major, enum fman_port_type type,
 			break;
 		case FMAN_PORT_TYPE_RX:
 			if (speed == 10000)
-				val = 96;
+				val = clamp_t(uint, fsl_fm_rx10g_fifo_kb, 24, 112) * 4;
 			else
 				val = 50;
 			break;
